Create a Comprehensive Order Management Skill System
Build a modular skill library for end-to-end order processing with the following architecture:
1. Master Orchestrator: vnom-order-processing

Acts as the main controller, coordinating all sub-skills
Manages workflow and error handling across the entire order processing pipeline

2. PDF Extraction: vnom-pdf-extraction

Extracts customer details and order line items from uploaded PDF order forms
Returns structured data to the master skill

3. Data Validation: vnom-order-validation

Validates extracted data using MCP tools:

read_customer_by_name to verify customer exists
read_item_by_name to verify all items exist


Error Handling: If customer or any item is not found, halt processing and return clear error message to user

4. Stock Availability Check: vnom-stock-check

Verifies sufficient inventory for all order items
If stock is insufficient, delegates to vnom-stock-exception skill
Returns availability status to master skill

5. Stock Exception Handling: vnom-stock-exception

Rule: If customer segment is "Education", allow partial order fulfillment with available stock
Rule: For all other segments, reject order and return error with item-level stock details

6. Discount Application: vnom-discount-policy

Applied after successful validation and stock confirmation
Rule: Education segment = 10% discount per item
Rule: Technology segment = 5% discount per item
Returns discount information for order creation

7. Reorder Monitoring: vnom-reorder-check

After successful order placement, checks if items trigger reorder thresholds
Includes reorder status in final summary

8. Response Generation: vnom-order-response

Creates professional email response for customer
Summarizes order details, applied discounts, and any relevant notes

Workflow Summary:
PDF Upload → Extract Data → Validate Customer/Items → Check Stock → Handle Exceptions → Apply Discounts → Create Order (MCP) → Check Reorders → Generate Email Response
Key Requirements:

Use MCP tools for all database operations
Implement clear error handling at each stage
Skills should be modular and reusable
Master skill should provide comprehensive user feedback throughout the process